MIT LICENSE — WEBSITE CODE
The MIT license in LICENSES/MIT.txt applies to:
- assets/site.css and assets/site.js;
- examples/sources/build.py and examples/sources/build-homepage-exercise.py;
- the functional HTML markup, inline CSS and JavaScript in index.html,
  404.html, downloads/index.html, examples/index.html,
  examples/english-basics/index.html, examples/maths-and-chemistry/index.html
  and licensing/index.html;
- technical documentation in README.md.

In HTML files, this grant covers structure and functionality, not embedded
editorial prose, exercise content, literary passages, artwork or branding.
Generic interface labels needed to operate the code are included in the MIT
grant. Layout, colors, styling and interactions may be reused and modified.
The content and brand policy imposes no additional conditions on MIT code.

CONTENT AND BRANDING
Rights in original website prose, exercises, illustrations and branding are
reserved except for the permissions in licensing/index.html, published at
https://parseh.io/licensing/. That policy permits normal website use and
sharing for discussion, education, reviews and promotion, including commercial
coverage. It does not claim ownership of third-party or public-domain material.
The original exercise content in examples/sources/*.md is not MIT-licensed.

EXCEPTIONS AND EXISTING RIGHTS
